claim.claim-text:
receiving the plurality of MR images (132);
converting the plurality of MR images (132) into a 3D volume image (200) defined in a 3D coordinate space;
performing semantic segmentation of an anterior commissure (AC) region, a posterior commissure (PC) region, and a third ventricle region in the 3D volume image (200) based on a pre-trained segmentation model (134) to generate a 3D mask image (136) labeled with the AC region, the PC region, and the third ventricle region;
labeling an AC point, which corresponds to a center of mass of the AC region, as the AC region and a PC point, which corresponds to a center of mass of the PC region, as the PC region, in the 3D mask image (136);
constructing a 3D volumetric image of the segmented third ventricle region based on the labeled 3D mask image (136); and
determining the MSP based on the 3D volumetric image of the third ventricle region,
wherein the MSP is defined by:

normalizing a plurality of pixels of each of a plurality of slices of the 3D volume image (200) to intensity values within a predetermined range;
extracting a set of the plurality of pixels from a center region of interest in each of the plurality of slices of the 3D volume image (200); and
segmenting the AC region, the PC region, and the third ventricle region of the normalized and extracted 3D volume image (200) based on the pre-trained segmentation model (134) to generate the 3D mask image (136) labeled with the AC region, the PC region, and the third ventricle region.

dividing the 3D volumetric image of the third ventricle region into a first portion and a second portion by a candidate plane starting from a skeleton of the 3D volumetric image of the third ventricle region;
determining whether the candidate plane symmetrically divides the 3D volumetric image based on a shape and a number of voxels in the first portion and a shape and a number of voxels of the second portion; and
upon determining that the candidate plane symmetrically divides the 3D volumetric image, designating the candidate plane as the MSP.

a processor (110) configured to:
receive the plurality of MR images (132);
convert the plurality of MR images (132) into a 3D volume image (200) defined in a 3D coordinate space;
perform semantic segmentation of an anterior commissure (AC) region, a posterior commissure (PC) region, and a third ventricle region in the 3D volume image (200) based on a pre-trained segmentation model (134) to generate a 3D mask image (136) labeled with the AC region, the PC region, and the third ventricle region;
label an AC point, which corresponds to a center of mass of the AC region, as the AC region and a PC point, which corresponds to a center of mass of the PC region, as the PC region, in the 3D mask image (136);
construct a 3D volumetric image of the segmented third ventricle region based on the labeled 3D mask image (136); and
determine the MSP based on the 3D volumetric image of the third ventricle region,

normalizing a plurality of pixels of each of a plurality of slices of the 3D volume image (200) to intensity values within a predetermined range;
extracting a set of the plurality of pixels from a region of interest in each of the plurality of slices of the 3D volume image (200); and
segmenting the AC region, the PC region, and the third ventricle region of the normalized and extracted 3D volume image (200) based on the pre-trained segmentation model (134) to generate the 3D mask image (136) labeled with the AC region, the PC region, and the third ventricle region.

dividing the 3D volumetric image of the third ventricle region by a candidate plane starting from a skeleton of the 3D volumetric image of the third ventricle region;
determining whether the candidate plane symmetrically divides the 3D volumetric image; and
upon determining that the candidate plane symmetrically divides the 3D volumetric image, designating the candidate plane as the MSP.
